# dhcpcd service identity.
#
# dhcpcd drops privileges to this user before it does anything else, and
# if the account does not exist it refuses to run at all. Nothing
# declared it: the upstream install target creates no account, the recipe
# installed the payload with a bare `make install`, and there is no
# sysusers.d fragment anywhere in the closure to replay.
#
# The result is worse than an obvious failure, because it is a SILENT
# one. saphira-network-config runs `dhcpcd -q <iface>`, which daemonises:
# the parent exits 0 the moment it forks, and the privileged child then
# prints "no such user dhcpcd" and dies. dhcpcd_up therefore saw success,
# the service reported "configured N interface definition(s)", the boot
# logged nothing red, and the machine came up with no address and no
# default route at all. A DHCP client that cannot start must not be able
# to report that it started.
#
# This is the same gap already fixed for frr, lldpd and mysql: the
# package configures a service account the package never declared, only
# quieter.
#
# ID IT NOT 157:  it is 104:104  check base seeds! do not assume an id is free
# the next free slot above the declared 100-199 package tier
# (sshd 101 ... polkitd 156), clear of the foundation identities.
user dhcpcd 104 dhcpcd /var/lib/dhcpcd /sbin/nologin
group dhcpcd 104
